Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:19:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Sandbox /leash: re-check after the cross-lock; prove each
 step it moves

From ChatGPT's C4d review:
- After locking leader and follower together, the tick checks again that
  it is still the follower's pending leash task and that the leader is
  online, so a cancelled or replaced tick does nothing (F2).
- unstick moves the follower only along a proved prefix of the route:
  outdoors a navmesh route between both ends (each within 2.5 m of the
  mesh), indoors a floor path in the same cell, and through a doorway
  only within the same building and 12 m. The warning names the reason
  when the way isn't proved (F1). walkable()/whyNotWalkable() are public
  so /agentpath can report the same proof.

Known open: some second hops outdoors are still refused ("no navmesh
route between the ends") where a path exists; under investigation.

Agent: Claude
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
